e of clearance against duty free categories /concessional duty categories, exemption / concession from duty shall be allowed.\n- CERTIFICATES 2.33 Warehousing Facility (a) Public / Private Customs Bonded Warehouses may be set up in DTA as per Chapter-IX of Customs Act, 1962, to import items in terms of Paragraph 2.36 of FTP.\n- CERTIFICATES\n- 4.41 Provisional clearance of export consignment Customs may allow provisional clearance of export consignment as and when Authorisation holder produces documentary evidence of having applied for Export Obligation ext...\n- GJEPC will forward the application after verification of bona fides with their clear recommendation for in principle approval of DGFT.\n\nSources:\n- HBP2023_Chapter04+as+on+20.04.2026.pdf | HBP Chapter 4 | 4.92 Export and import of Diamond, Gemstone & Jewellery on | Pages 53\n- HBP2023_Chapter04+as+on+20.04.2026.pdf | HBP Chapter 4 | 4.77 Export Procedure/Payment of Customs Duty | Pages 44, 45, 46\n- HBP-Chapter-6.pdf | HBP Chapter 6 | 6.27 Personal Carriage of Import / Export Parcels including | Pages 15, 16\n- HBP-Chapter-6.pdf | HBP Chapter 6 | 6.39 Fast Track Clearance Procedure | Pages 22\n- HBP Chapter 2.pdf | HBP Chapter 2 | 2.33 Warehousing Facility | Pages 12"}
