], "matchedQueries": ["FTP Chapter 5"]}], "selected_chunk": ["2.97-1"], "final_prompt": "Question: What is EPCG?\nDetected intent: EPCG\nDetected entities: what, is, epcg, Chapter 5, FTP, chapter\nSelected sections: 5.01 Policy, 5.03 Nexus Certification, 2.97 Application to EPCG Committee, 5.25 Clubbing of EPCG authorisations\nSelected chunks: 2.97-1, 5.01-1, 5.25-1", "llm_response": "Based on the uploaded documents:\n- 5.01 Policy Policy relating to EPCG Scheme is given in Chapter 5 of FTP.\n- 5.03 Nexus Certification (a) RA concerned shall, on the basis of nexus certificate from an independent Chartered Engineer (CEC) submitted by the applicant in Appendix 5A, issue EPCG authorisation.\n- 2.97 Application to EPCG Committee (a) Application to the Export Promotion Capital Goods (EPCG) Committee under Para 2.59 of FTP is to be made online in ANF-2D with the prescribed fee in terms of Appendix-2K with requ...\n- 5.25 Clubbing of EPCG authorisations (a) Clubbing of two or more EPCG authorisations issued to the same authorisation holder would be permitted.\n\nKey requirements:\n- Representative(s) from concerned line Ministry / Department may be co-opted as member, as and when required.\n- 5.03 Nexus Certification (a) RA concerned shall, on the basis of nexus certificate from an independent Chartered Engineer (CEC) submitted by the applicant in Appendix 5A, issue EPCG authorisation.\n- For issuance of such certificate, the Chartered Engineer shall act only in the domain of his/her competence.\n- In case of fabrication, reasonable wastage, if any, anticipated at the time of installation of capital goods shall be certified by the Chartered Engineer in the nexus certificate and the same would be mentioned in the...\n- (b) An application for amendment in the list of import item(s) including addition(s)/deletion(s), if any, may be filed with RA concerned provided the authorisation is valid for import.\n- The applicant would give justification for seeking such amendment(s) along with fresh nexus certificate from an independent Chartered Engineer.\n\nSources:\n- HBP2023_Chapter05.pdf | HBP Chapter 5 | 5.01 Policy | Pages 2\n- HBP2023_Chapter05.pdf | HBP Chapter 5 | 5.03 Nexus Certification | Pages 2\n- HBP Chapter 2.pdf | HBP Chapter 2 | 2.97 Application to EPCG Committee | Pages 52\n- HBP2023_Chapter05.pdf | HBP Chapter 5 | 5.25 Clubbing of EPCG authorisations | Pages 14, 15"}
